- NekoBox for Android, https://github.com/MatsuriDayo/NekoBoxForAndroid: GPL-3.0, MatsuriDayo
- SagerNet, https://github.com/SagerNet/SagerNet: GPL-3.0, Copyright (C) 2021 nekohasekai
- sing-box, https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-box, and sing-quic: GPL-3.0, Copyright (C) 2022 nekohasekai
- sing-box-lx, https://github.com/Leadaxe/sing-box-lx (XHTTP, REALITY changes): GPL-3.0, Leadaxe
- shadowsocks-android, https://github.com/shadowsocks/shadowsocks-android: GPL-3.0


What the app carries, with its own license
------------------------------------------

The texts of these licenses, with each holder's copyright, are in the APK under assets/licenses/: go.json for the
core's Go modules (from the build), components.json and texts/ for the rest (app:checkLicenses holds them to the
build's runtime libraries).

The core (libcore.aar, libgojni.so)
  The Go modules a build links in are the ones its own build info lists (`go version -m`): the build writes them,
  with the license files of each, into the APK as assets/licenses/go.json (buildScript/lib/core/licenses.py). Most
  are under GPL-3.0, MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0 or ISC. Of the others:
  - yggdrasil-go (the fork https://github.com/arngory/yggdrasil-go): LGPL-3.0 with a linking exception
  - ironwood, phony, yamux: MPL-2.0, used unchanged at the versions libcore/go.mod names
  - dnstt: CC0-1.0; aurora: Unlicense
  - the Go runtime and standard library: BSD-3-Clause, Copyright The Go Authors

Chromium (naive's network stack, libcronet in libgojni.so)
  Chromium of the release the library modules of cronet-go carry, built from https://github.com/arngory/naiveproxy
  at the commit the cronet-go commit libcore/go.mod takes names as its submodule (branch niko; the release's
  SOURCES.md says which): BSD-3-Clause, Copyright The Chromium Authors, and the licenses of the third-party code
  it contains (BoringSSL, zlib, brotli and others). The modules carry Chromium's own credits of all of them,
  NOTICE.chromium.txt, which go.json holds with the modules' other files.

The slipstream client (libslipstream.so)
  https://github.com/arngory/slipstream: Apache-2.0. It contains picoquic (MIT, Copyright (c) 2017 Private
  Octopus), picotls (MIT, Copyright (c) 2016 DeNA Co., Ltd., Kazuho Oku), OpenSSL (Apache-2.0),
  lua-resty-base-encoding (MIT), quick_arg_parser (MIT, Copyright (c) 2021 Dugy) and SPCDNS (LGPL-3.0, Copyright
  2010 by Sean Conner).
  SPCDNS is linked statically: the source of the client and of SPCDNS at the commits above and the build script
  (buildScript/lib/slipstream/build.sh) are public, so the client can be rebuilt with a modified SPCDNS and put in
  place of the one in the app.

Rule databases (assets/sing-box/geoip.db, geosite.db)
  From https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-geoip and https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-geosite (GPL-3.0). geoip.db is
  made from https://github.com/Dreamacro/maxmind-geoip: this product includes GeoLite2 data created by MaxMind,
  available from https://www.maxmind.com. geosite.db is made from
  https://github.com/v2fly/domain-list-community (MIT).

The Clash API dashboard (assets/yacd.zip)
  Yacd-meta, https://github.com/MetaCubeX/Yacd-meta, a fork of yacd, https://github.com/haishanh/yacd: MIT.

